From afb3e63e0c1ff99e8295133806818a92c5724ed1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 18:54:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 062/113] rust: drm: add typed RAII event channels

Add event delivery for a concrete DRM driver/file pair. A connection token owns the logical receiver and disconnects automatically on drop.

Reserve a private pending-event anchor for each connection. DRM core clears the anchor's file pointer under event_lock during close, so send can test and queue under the same lock without retaining an untyped or dangling drm_file pointer. The channel stores the exact DRM device and never accepts an arbitrary device at send time.

This replaces the erased, manually closed EventChannel from the local v2 series; it intentionally omits the unsound with_receiver type-erasure escape.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
---
